        "summary": "tests.yml triggers on push to main and on pull_request, runs on ubuntu-latest with a 3.11 / 3.x matrix, checks out, sets up Python, and runs unittest discovery. It omits the README's PATH prefix on purpose: that prefix keeps a local interpreter shim off PATH, and on the runner it would put the system python3 ahead of the matrix interpreter. No apt step: the suite fakes every desktop tool, and the only real binaries it reaches are patch and cat, both preinstalled.",
